          <Pad Id="FdFOudnQVRNLWAU2u30epY" Bounds="107,513,173,62" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="↑ Stride Texture&#xD;&#xA;↓ Skia&#xD;&#xA;">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="V0X5Uu5S78ONKqaNqcMaJo" Bounds="391,52,581,742" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Creating Images for Skia Using Stride&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;That is the beginning... The idea is that we import an image into the 2D drawing enviroment of skia. The image could be a static image and there are helppatches for that.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;However, it is also possible to create images from scratch. To do so, we can generate a texture inside Stride, the 3D game engine used by vvvv gamma, and then convert it into a format that Skia can draw.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;You can think of texture generation in Stride as being similar to a chain of Photoshop filters. Textures can be combined, modified, and animated at any stage of the pipeline, giving complete control over their appearance and behaviour.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The patch works as follows:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;1. Create a Base Texture: A texture filled with a uniform white colour is created.Hover over the second input pin to see that the texture resolution is set to 512 × 512 pixels.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;2. Create a Circle Texture: A second texture is generated containing a white circle on a black background. It uses the same resolution as the base texture.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;3. Convert the Texture Data: The ColorMap and Convert nodes transform the image into an array of four-dimensional vectors (RGBA values) that can be processed directly on the GPU.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;4. Apply an Alpha Mask: The circle texture is used as an alpha mask. Pixels outside the circle are black and therefore become fully transparent, while the white pixels remain opaque.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;5. Convert Texture to Image: In vvvv gamma, a Texture and an Image are different data types. The TextureToImage node converts the GPU texture into a Stride image.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;6. Convert from Stride to Skia: The image is then converted from a Stride image into a Skia image.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;This is effectively the point where we switch from the Stride rendering environment to the Skia drawing environment.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;7. Draw the Image: Finally, the image is displayed on the Skia canvas using the DrawImage node.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;At this point, the image behaves like any other image in Skia and can be combined with text, vector graphics, or additional drawing operations.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
